WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:11.480
When Dr. Henderson was assigning project mates for his psychology class, I secretly hoped he would pair me with my best friend or at least a classmate I could have some fun with.
亨德森博士给他的心理学课指定项目搭档时，我暗暗希望他把我和最好的朋友分在一组，至少也分给我一个能一起玩得开心的同学。

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:22.440
Above all, I hoped he wouldn’t assign me to work with the fiercely competitive, extremely serious fellow who always wore dark clothes and apparently had a personality to match.
最重要的是，我希望他别安排我和那个家伙一起做——他好胜心极强、极其严肃，总穿深色衣服，看样子性格也和衣服一样阴沉。

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:32.990
As fate would have it, Dr. Henderson very deliberately matched everyone in class and announced that I would be working with the one person in class I wanted to avoid.
偏偏天意弄人，亨德森博士十分用心地给班上每个人配好了对，还宣布我将和班上我唯一想躲开的那个人合作。

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:36.550
I went up to my new teammate and introduced myself.
我走到新搭档跟前，作了自我介绍。

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.210
He looked at me as though I weren’t there.
他看着我，就好像我不存在一样。

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:45.800
I felt he treated me as though I would hold him back and probably make him fail to get an A in the course.
我觉得他对待我的样子，仿佛我会拖他后腿，没准还会害他这门课拿不到A。

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:54.050
He wasn’t mean or abusive; he just gave me the impression he could do whatever project we dreamed up better if he did it alone.
他并不刻薄，也没有恶语相向；他只是给我一种印象：不管我们想出什么项目，他自己一个人做都会做得更好。

00:00:54.850 --> 00:01:04.310
Needless to say, I didn’t look forward to an entire term of being brushed off, but I tried to make the best of it and didn’t say anything for fear that I would make things worse.
不用说，我可不盼着整整一个学期都被人冷落，但我还是尽量随遇而安，什么也没说，生怕把事情弄得更糟。

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:14.600
The project required each team to develop a hypothesis, set up an experiment to test the hypothesis, do the statistical analysis and present the findings.
这个项目要求每个小组提出一个假说，设计实验来检验它，做统计分析，并展示研究结果。

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:18.790
Whatever grade the team received would be shared by both students.
小组得到的分数不论高低，都由两名学生共享。

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:23.570
When my teammate and I met to discuss our project, I was uneasy.
我和搭档碰面讨论项目时，心里很不安。

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:31.430
Here was this challenging student who had a reputation for single-mindedness and good grades—the exact opposite of me.
眼前就是这个难对付的同学，他出了名的一心一意、成绩优秀——和我恰恰相反。

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:33.300
I was outmatched.
我根本不是他的对手。

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:41.290
I actually wanted to drop the class at one point, but stopped short because I didn’t want to give him the satisfaction of my chickening out.
有一阵子我真想退掉这门课，但最后还是忍住了，因为我不想让他看到我临阵退缩而暗自得意。

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:44.170
I decided to stick to it no matter what.
我下定决心，无论如何都要坚持下去。

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:50.720
After long discussions we somehow agreed to do a study on the psychological well-being of teenagers.
讨论了很久之后，我们总算同意做一项关于青少年心理健康的研究。

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:55.080
I wasn’t sure what it meant exactly, but at least we had a topic.
我不太清楚它确切指什么，但至少我们有了题目。

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:58.600
We started to meet regularly to draw up our plans.
我们开始定期碰面，拟订计划。

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:03.910
One day I got word that he was admitted to hospital for a serious disease.
有一天，我得到消息，他因患重病住院了。
